{
	"_doc": {
		"what": "Reference v83 monster strength by level: for levels 1-200 (index = level - 1) the HP, weapon attack (pad), magic attack (mad), weapon defence (pdd), magic defence (mdd) and EXP of an ordinary monster of that level. A stage's level_scale divides one level's value by another to rescale a monster (RunWorld, LevelScale).",
		"tier": "A-derived numbers (v83 Mob.wz info: maxHP, PADamage, MADamage, PDDamage, MDDamage, exp), used for a tier C purpose.",
		"source": "the owner's v83 Mob.wz, read with `wzimport dump Mob.wz --imgs 2`",
		"generator": "tools/level_curve/generate.mjs (tools/level_curve/run.sh); same dump and date give the same bytes",
		"date": "2026-10-30",
		"method": [
			"1. Ordinary monsters: not boss=1; not an info/link mob without stances; a mainline field monster, Mob.wz id below 9000000 (ids from 9000000 are party-quest, carnival, event, trial, GM and later-client content, docs/research/v83-bosses.md 'Excluded'), without the Balrog variants 6400005-6400009 and the Zakum, Horntail and Pink Bean bodies 8800000-8899999; level 1-200 with maxHP above 0.",
			"2. HP outliers: a mob whose maxHP is above 5x the median maxHP of its level is dropped.",
			"3. Per level and stat, the median of the remaining mobs' values; a mob whose value is 0 is skipped for that stat (a mob without magic attack has MADamage 0, which says nothing about its level's magic damage).",
			"4. Levels with no sample are filled by log-linear interpolation between the nearest sampled levels; below the first and above the last sampled level the nearest value holds.",
			"5. Made monotone non-decreasing by weighted isotonic regression on the log values (pool adjacent violators; a level weighs its sample count, an interpolated level 0.25), smoothed with the weights 1-2-1 over neighbouring levels on the log values (edges repeat; smoothing keeps a monotone curve monotone), rounded to two decimals."
		],
